{
  "requirement": "Each requirement and example declaration badge has two adjacent links. Its\nkind (`req` or `example`) links to the declaration's anchor on the current\npage; its full name links to the evidence detail page. These segments stay\ntogether in one non-wrapping row, with no separate arrow link or plaintext evidence link.\nEach detail page links back to the declaration's anchored badge and to the\nindex. Reference badges continue to link to the declaration. These links\nresolve when a requirement name contains `.md`, as in\n`requirements.cli.mdbook`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.index.navigation`.\n\n**Declaration badge, two adjacent links**\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[declaration_sections_contain_their_headers_and_markdown_bodies]` checks the header of both a req and an example declaration.\n  - The kind link has `href=\"#habeas-{kind}-rules.{name}\"`, the title \"Link to … in this chapter\", and the aria-label.\n  - The name link has `href=\"requirements-index/rules.{name}.html\"` and the title \"View evidence for …\".\n  - Both links sit inside the `<summary>` header, not the body.\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[definition_evidence_link_targets_are_escaped]` checks that the name-link href is escaped and relative to the index path.\n- `tests/repository.rs#fn[mdbook_preprocessor_renders_definitions_between_stdin_and_stdout]` runs the real preprocessor end to end. It checks that each badge row has a kind link and a name link, with exactly 2 `</a>` per row, and that both targets are `#habeas-req-rules.ready` and `requirements-index/rules.ready.html`.\n\n**One non-wrapping row, no arrow link or plaintext evidence link**\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[declaration_badge_stylesheet_keeps_split_links_in_one_row]` asserts `inline-flex`, `flex-wrap: nowrap`, `white-space: nowrap` and `flex-shrink: 0`.\n- The header assertions `!habeas-detail-icon`, `!<svg` and `!See evidence` appear in `fn[declaration_sections_contain_their_headers_and_markdown_bodies]`, `fn[declaration_badges_and_margin_controls_share_kind_colors]`, `fn[index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons]` and the repository test. The two-`</a>` count in the repository test also rules out a third link.\n\n**Detail pages link back to the badge and the index**\n- `src/index.rs#mod[tests]/fn[index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters]` asserts `[View definition](../../requirements/core.html#habeas-req-requirements.core.ready)` and `[Requirements index](../requirements-index.html) · [View definition]`.\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages]` checks the index link and the definition link on every detail page, including a nested chapter.\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons]` checks a detail page's definition link when the index sits in a different directory.\n- `src/index.rs#mod[tests]/fn[detail_pages_link_to_readme_chapters_at_their_index_output]` covers README chapters.\n- `fn[detail_pages_rebase_markdown_links_and_images_from_the_definition]` also carries the navigation marker. Its link-rebasing assertions are about body content, not these navigation obligations.\n\n**Reference badges still link to the declaration**\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[references_in_nested_chapters_link_to_the_requirement_definition]` asserts the impl, cite and test badges each have `href=\"../requirements.html#habeas-req-requirements.ready\"`.\n\n**Names containing `.md`**\n- `fn[links_preserve_requirement_names_containing_md]` and `fn[links_to_readme_chapters_use_the_index_output]` assert exact `%2Emd` output from `chapter_href`.\n- Both the badge links and the detail-page links assert `%2Emd` for `cli.mdbook`: in `fn[definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages]` (id, href, evidence link and View-definition link) and in `fn[index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons]`.\n- No test renders a reference badge whose target name contains `.md`. `reference_badge` builds its href with the same `chapter_href` that those tests cover, and that function applies the `%2Emd` replacement to the whole href, anchor included. I treat this as covered.\n\n**Gaps and acknowledgments**\n- I found no unacknowledged gap, and the task has no acknowledgments.",
  "references": "c695497dc38e4a206fcdcbcdf19c6f99199afeef8d23c602364dc4aeef8b31d6",
